title 52V pack running flat at level 9: resting voltage falls 47.5V to 44.5V over 60 s, 0.15 ohm sag

# The pack sags by current x resistance, so limiting power also shrinks the
# sag. A low-voltage limit that reacts to the voltage it causes can hunt;
# this scenario checks it settles, and that power still goes down as the
# pack genuinely empties.
config max_battery_x100v 5880
config low_cut_off_v 42
bike battery_r 0.15

at 0 level 9
at 0 voltage 47.5
at 1000 cadence 70 over 500
at 5000 voltage 44.5 over 60000
at 70000 cadence 0

end 72000

# Power falls steadily as the pack empties, with no hunting: swings stay
# within a percent or two (upstream behaved the same here).
expect 20000 current == 61
expect 40000 current == 45
expect 70000 current == 25
